<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Vráž–Svatý Jan pod Skalou–Karlštejn — Complete Vráž–Svatý Jan–Karlštejn railway traverse</name><desc>From Vráž u Berouna station, follow green then yellow markings to Svatý Jan pod Skalou and the public Ivan spring approach beside the church. Climb the marked path to the cross on Svatojánská skála, then retrace to the red-trail junction. Continue through Propadlé vody and Bubovické waterfalls past Kubrychtova bouda, Králova studně and Dub sedmi bratří to Karlštejn castle. Follow the pedestrian village and bridge approach to the station underpass. Carry drinking water: Ivan spring is not safe to drink. Stay on marked reserve paths and public ground; monastery and castle interiors are separate visits.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright).

